Personally, I think that the new version tends to be too hard.
The problem is that you can do fine for a while, and suddenly one
creature will kill you in two rounds. Another thing is that altars,
for their importance in the game, are a bit too rare.
On the other hand, it's sort of nice to have a bit of a challenge
occasionally...

And no, I'm not one of these totally-inept by nature players. I've been
playing hack of various sorts since before nethack was invented. 3.0 is
the first one in about 5 years that's been a nice challenge.

As to directions for bows, etc:
Why not do what omega does, and let people target effects? This would only work
for knives and bows, and things like that. Things that have a bolt-type effect
could stay with the 8-dir function.

As to eating: How about, when you get attacked, *asking* if you want to stop?
For instance, if I've got a working Elbereth under me, it would be nice if I
could just open the ****ing tin, instead of stopping all the time, and it would
also be nice if I had the option of stopping eating my food ration when I see
the crowd of orks. Used to be there was ^A to abort a command in progress...

Also, why don't we make Elbereth a *little* more reliable... After all, creatures
with missile weapons can still ignore it, so it's not all that safe...

Apart from that, though, it's a fun game.
Myself, I've compiled it (I set it up here... with some help from rabe, who
posted a while back) so that it puts saves in people's $HOME, and I let people
make backup saves and all that *without* using discover mode. That way, people
can get decent scores and all that.

